  {
   "id": "cap-bcl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": -1450,
   "width": 2600,
   "height": 64,
   "text": "routed experts 288×42 **8.46B** (50.5%) · KDA linear attention ×34 **4.68B** (28.0%) · MLA attention ×11 **1.29B** (7.7%) · shared expert + router ×42 **1.11B** (6.6%) · dense FFN ×3 **453.0M** (2.7%) · lm head **634.4M** (3.8%) · DSA indexers ×11 **82.2M** (0.5%) · mHC mixers ×90 **35.4M** (0.2%) · embed **0** (row lookup) · MTP block **0** (only when drafting) · ViT + merger **0** (runs per image) · norms **373K** (<0.1%)"
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-title",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": -1300,
   "width": 1250,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "# GLM-5.3-Flash — model  \nOne continuous decoder stack L0–44, read top → bottom; layers that repeat are drawn once with **×N**. **Grey bars = tensors**, length ∝ channels per token (0.08 px/channel). **Boxes = operations**, all one size; where parameters and compute live is the pair of bars above. T = sequence length. *Layer* tab = one decoder layer in detail (both token mixers)."
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-legend",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 450,
   "y": -1300,
   "width": 1250,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "Row colours — **cyan**: KDA linear attention (64 heads, fixed 128×128 state per head) + MoE · **amber**: KDA + dense SwiGLU FFN (L0–2) · **orange**: MLA made sparse by **DSA** — each query attends only the top 2048 past tokens picked by its own indexer — + MoE. Layout = 11 × (3 KDA + 1 DSA) + 1 KDA.    \nMoE = 8 of 288 routed experts + 1 shared, sigmoid router. The residual stream is **4 lanes** wide (mHC); each sub-layer reads a weighted mix of the lanes and writes back into all of them."
  },
  {
