  {
   "id": "note-mix",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -620,
   "y": -419,
   "width": 460,
   "height": 330,
   "text": "**Why mix the two?** A KDA layer keeps one 128×128 matrix per head (64 heads) and updates it token by token, so its memory and compute per token stay flat however long the context.    \nA DSA layer caches a 512-value MLA latent + a 257-value indexer entry per past token.    \nAt 1,048,576 tokens: 11 DSA layers ≈ **17.7 GB** cache (bf16) vs 34 KDA layers ≈ **143 MB** state (fp32)."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-pos",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 540,
   "y": -259,
   "width": 600,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "**No positional encoding in the LLM.** qk_rope_head_dim = 0: MLA keys and queries are all \"nope\" (256 dims/head) and the forward passes no RoPE. Token order comes from KDA's causal conv (4 taps) and recurrence. Only the ViT uses (2-D) RoPE. Context 1,048,576 positions."
  },
  {
   "id": "img11",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1250,
   "y": -980,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**image / video** frames",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "patch12",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1147,
