   "height": 34,
   "text": "`[T, 4096]`"
  },
  {
   "id": "mblk42",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2750,
   "y": 850,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**1 decoder layer** — MLA + own indexer + MoE 8/288, no mHC  \n7.40B · incl. norms",
   "color": "#f59e0b"
  },
  {
   "id": "mhead43",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2750,
   "y": 946,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**shared_head.norm → lm head** (main's)",
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "mdraft44",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2880,
   "y": 1042,
   "width": 40,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl45",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 3070,
   "y": 1030,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`draft token t+2`"
  },
  {
   "id": "mver46",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2750,
   "y": 1091,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**verify**: main model checks the draft in its next forward",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-mtp",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2750,
   "y": 1177,
   "width": 600,
   "height": 140,
   "text": "MTP = multi-token prediction (1 block, 7.43B stored). Trained to predict one token further; serving stacks use it as a speculative-decoding draft. Not part of transformers' Glm5NextForConditionalGeneration — wiring read from its tensor names (no embed / head of its own, and no hc_* tensors, so it runs on a single 4096-wide stream)."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-src",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": 1387,
   "width": 1300,
   "height": 150,
   "text": "**Sources.** config.json + safetensors headers of zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash (76108 tensors). FP8 E4M3 in 128×128 blocks for experts, dense/shared FFNs and MLA projections (314.40B params; scales not counted); KDA, indexers, mHC, embed, head and ViT stay BF16. Main model (L0–44, embed, head) = **313.33B**, +7.43B MTP, +563.6M vision. Dataflow from transformers modeling_glm5_next.py."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-big",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": 1567,
   "width": 1300,
   "height": 170,
   "text": "**vs GLM-5.3** (the big sibling, 753B): 78 → 45 layers, hidden 6144 → 4096, 256 → 288 routed experts (still top-8 + 1 shared). GLM-5.3 runs MLA+DSA in every layer with RoPE on 64 dims and lets 57 layers reuse another layer's top-k; Flash makes 34 of 45 layers KDA linear attention, drops RoPE, gives each DSA layer its own indexer scoring 4-token pools, widens the residual into 4 mHC lanes and adds a ViT for images and video."
  }
 ],
